# Design and picture commitment proposal

The objective is a 20-second film, The Paper Lantern: at dusk a child releases a paper lantern onto a river, it passes the village, and becomes a small light among the stars. Four to six still-image-based shots; 1280x720 at 24 fps; opening title and end card. Final H.264/AAC stereo export belongs to edit, with water/evening ambience and soft music, no dialogue.

I own the design and all shot picture. Proposed delivered paths: `design/` and `picture/`. I supply source stills, finished silent shot clips, shot timing/camera-move log and reference release. Director supplies approved beats, framing intent, shot count/timing and title-safe requirements; editor supplies typography/card treatment, timeline, transitions, sound and final MP4. If editor prefers animating supplied stills, agree that explicitly before production to keep picture ownership clear.

Proposed treatment for direction to settle: quiet hand-painted storybook imagery, soft textured gouache, indigo water, dusty rose horizon, warm amber lantern; a small child with short dark bob, rust-red coat, dark blue trousers; one cuboid ivory paper lantern with four slender dark ribs, warm amber light, shallow dark wooden floating base. No dangling sky-lantern geometry. Village is a small timeless riverside settlement of plaster walls, tiled roofs and amber windows.

Proposed five visual beats: (1) river/village establishing view with child and lantern, leaving title space; (2) low close view of child's hands at the water and released floating lantern; (3) lantern drifting beside village reflections; (4) broader river with receding lantern and growing star field; (5) final small amber point against reflected and overhead stars, leaving end-card space. Exact shots and lengths await direction.

No production imagery has been made yet; assignment and direction are not yet present. Acceptance evidence will distinguish observed frames and measured media from planned intent.
